    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_1e6325b9",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "immigration_wall_politics",
      "label": "U.S. immigration wall policy",
      "description": "The meme references the real-world political debate and policy proposals in the United States regarding the construction of a border wall, particularly along the southern border, as a means of controlling immigration. This policy has been a major point of contention in U.S. politics, especially during the presidency of Donald Trump, and is often associated with rhetoric about 'keeping people out' and national security.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_ba9c2380"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_0b301cd8",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "anti_latino_stereotype",
      "label": "Anti-Latino/Hispanic stereotypes",
      "description": "The meme relies on the stereotype that Latinos are 'coming in' or 'invading' the U.S., often associated with the idea of them being 'outsiders' or 'invaders' who should be kept out. This stereotype is commonly used in political discourse and media to frame immigration as a threat, and it is often linked to negative portrayals of Latinos as criminals, job stealers, or 'anchor babies'.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_ba9c2380"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_e33e3405",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "taco_bell_cultural_reference",
      "label": "Taco Bell as a cultural symbol of American fast food",
      "description": "Taco Bell is a widely recognized fast-food chain in the United States, often associated with American culture and the fast-food industry. Its presence in the meme is used to create a humorous or ironic juxtaposition with the serious topic of immigration and border walls, implying that the 'wall' is meant to keep out people who are 'coming in' to places like Taco Bell, which is a common cultural touchstone.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_ba9c2380"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_0aabc8ea",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "xenophobia",
      "label": "Xenophobia",
      "description": "The meme implicitly references xenophobia, which is the fear or dislike of people from other countries or cultures. The phrase 'build a wall to keep yall out' is a direct reference to xenophobic attitudes, suggesting that the wall is meant to exclude people who are perceived as 'foreign' or 'different'. This is a common theme in political rhetoric and can be used to justify exclusionary policies.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_ba9c2380"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_5f2e39cf",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "slang_usage",
      "label": "Use of informal and regional slang",
      "description": "The text in the meme uses informal and regional slang, such as 'gunna' and 'yall', which are common in American English, particularly in Southern dialects. This slang is used to create a casual, conversational tone that is often associated with everyday American speech, which helps to frame the meme as a humorous or satirical comment rather than a formal political statement.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_ba9c2380"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_5d4cd31a",
      "@type": "EmotionExpression",
      "instance_name": "mockery",
      "label": "mocking emotion",
      "description": "The emotion expressed is mockery, conveyed through the satirical juxtaposition of a fast-food restaurant with the serious political concept of a border wall, implying that immigrants are 'coming in' to places like Taco Bell and should be kept out. The use of informal slang ('gunna', 'yall') and the absurdity of the scenario contribute to the mocking tone.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_ba9c2380"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_0268ea10",
      "@type": "AnalogicalMapping",
      "instance_name": "mapping_1",
      "label": "Taco Bell as the target of the wall",
      "description": "The text 'build a wall to keep yall out' is mapped onto the Taco Bell restaurant, implying that the wall is meant to keep out people who are 'coming in' to this fast-food establishment. This creates an analogical mapping where the visual entity (Taco Bell restaurant) is projected as the 'place' that needs to be protected by the wall, as described in the text.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_ba9c2380"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_e4fdc20a",
      "@type": "SemioticProjection",
      "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
      "label": "User projected onto the textual material",
      "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material because the text uses second-person pronouns ('you americans', 'yall') which directly address the viewer, creating an implicit 'you' as the projected user. The user is invited to imagine themselves as part of the group being addressed ('you americans') and is positioned as the one who would react to the scenario described ('what you americans guna do when they build a wall').",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_ba9c2380"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_ef37305b",
      "@type": "ToxicityAssessment",
      "instance_name": "toxicity_1",
      "label": "Harmful",
      "description": "The meme uses a satirical and provocative image to mock or joke about U.S. immigration policy by juxtaposing a border wall with a fast-food restaurant, implying that immigrants are 'coming in' to places like Taco Bell and should be kept out. This reinforces negative stereotypes about immigrants and can contribute to xenophobic attitudes, even if presented as a joke. The overall intent is to provoke a reaction through humor that may be offensive or divisive, potentially causing harm by normalizing or trivializing immigration-related tensions.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_ba9c2380"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_bf75ec8e",
      "@type": "TargetCommunity",
      "instance_name": "audience_id",
      "label": "American audience",
      "description": "The meme is designed for a general American audience familiar with U.S. immigration politics, fast-food culture, and colloquial American English. The use of slang like 'gunna' and 'yall', the reference to Taco Bell as a cultural touchstone, and the satirical framing of a border wall joke all signal that the target community is American citizens or residents who understand the political and cultural context. The meme relies on American-specific stereotypes and humor to resonate with this demographic.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_ba9c2380"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
